# Rust
/target
**/target
# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
# Both lockfiles are committed deliberately, not ignored: `uv run` inside a directory
# with a `[project]` pyproject.toml resolves the project and writes uv.lock, exactly as
# `cargo` reads Cargo.lock — both are needed for each binding's CI to be reproducible.
# NEVER ignore generated bindings — they are committed on purpose so consumers need no
# code-generation toolchain (see README "What this is").
